 tion_vegetable-printing\n\nOpen to Stanford students\, staff\, faculty\, a
 nd affiliates.\n\nJoin us at Craft the Collection: Vegetable Printing & Re
 lief Embroidery Workshop! 🥔🪡🎨🌱\n\nInspired by In Focus: Asian 
 American Art from the Collection\, our inaugural Craft the Collection Work
 shop invites you to explore the Cantor’s collection through hands-on mak
 ing. Drawing inspiration from Ruth Asawa’s vegetable printing and Pacita
  Abad’s trapunto textile work\, we invite you to explore the artists’ 
 techniques.\n\nCarve your own vegetable stamps\, experiment with colorful 
 prints\, and try your hand at relief embroidery to customize a free tote b
 ag or your own textiles.\n\nStop by for snacks and refreshments and discov
 er new ways to engage with the Cantor’s collection beyond the gallery wa
 lls.\n\nCome for the crafts\, stay for the community. We can’t wait to s
 ee what you make!\n\nMust be affiliated with Stanford to participate.​ R
 SVP here.\n\nWarmly\,\nThe Cantor Student Advisory Committee\n\n________\n
